# Tests — `test/controllers`

## Role

- Exercise HTTP entry points: status, redirects, assigns, `flash`, cookie behavior, and Turbo responses (`format.turbo_stream`) when relevant.

## Strategy

- Per action: success (200/302/303 per convention) and business failure (422/403/404) — maximize surface to catch silent 500s.
- Auth/scope: simulate expected user/role (`sign_in`, project helpers) without duplicating policy suites if a dedicated layer exists.
- Assigns/scope: assert main instance variables via `assigns(...)` when they encode scope/authorization.
- Params: cover nominal path; assert invalid params are rejected clearly — not every combination.
- Don’t re-test every `before_action` everywhere if covered elsewhere — useful signal is “this action does not 500”.

## Integration vs controller

- If complex logic lives in a service: controller test asserts delegation + response; business detail belongs in `test/services`.
